WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:09.267
In this walkthrough we'll see how a
market curve is defined, and what it
depends on, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:17.633
The Curve Viewer showed a curve. The Market Index
Manager is where that curve is defined in the first place.

3
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:29.167
Indexes are catalogued by type. Discount
curves, overnight index curves, and
composites built from others, each with its own currency.

4
00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:41.433
An index carries metadata rather than numbers. The
market it belongs to, the group it sits in, and
how values between published points are interpolated.

5
00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:51.367
Holiday calendars attach here, which is
how a curve knows which days are good
business days for the currency it prices.

6
00:00:51.367 --> 00:01:02.767
Dependencies are the interesting part. A
composite index is built from others, so
changing one of those changes everything downstream of it.

7
00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:16.733
New index adds a definition to the catalogue. Once it
exists and has grid point data published against it, it
becomes selectable in the Curve Viewer and usable by valuations.

8
00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:26.867
That completes Market Indexes and Curves. Every
surface shown here can also be opened from the
agent panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
